##INFO=<ID=ClinVar_ONCSCV,Number=.,Type=String,Description="SCV accession numbers for the submissions that contribute to the aggregate oncogenicity classification in ClinVar; multiple values are separated by a vertical bar. Values are separated by + and percent-encoded, so that they survive ingestion as a VEP custom annotation.. ONCSCV field from [PATH]/clinvar.vcf.gz">
##INFO=<ID=ClinVar_ONCCONF,Number=.,Type=String,Description="Conflicting oncogenicity classification for this single variant; multiple values are separated by a vertical bar. Values are separated by + and percent-encoded, so that they survive ingestion as a VEP custom annotation.. ONCCONF field from [PATH]/clinvar.vcf.gz">
##INFO=<ID=ClinVar_CLNSUBA,Number=.,Type=String,Description="Per-submission detail from the ClinVar VCV XML, one entry per SCV, separated by commas. Subfields separated by ~: SCV | Submitter | OrgID | OrgCategory | DateLastEvaluated | ReviewStatus | ClassificationType | Classification | ClinicalImpact | Method | Origin | AffectedStatus | Condition | ConditionID | PMID | Contributes | RCV. Contributes is 1 when the submission contributes to the aggregate classification for its statement type and 0 when it does not. RCV is the accession this submission belongs to, taken from the RCV release, which states the grouping explicitly; it cannot be derived from condition names or MedGen concepts, which disagree between the two levels. Multiple values within a subfield are separated by +. Spaces are rendered as underscores and the characters comma, semicolon, equals, pipe, ampersand, tilde, plus and percent are percent-encoded within values. VEP rewrites both comma and pipe to ampersand in a custom annotation, so after VEP the separator between entries reads as & instead of , while the ~ and + levels are unchanged.. CLNSUBA field from [PATH]/clinvar.vcf.gz">
##INFO=<ID=ClinVar_CLNPMID,Number=.,Type=String,Description="PubMed IDs cited as evidence for this variant in the ClinVar XML (aggregate-level citations plus per-submission classification and observation citations). Assertion-method and disease-review citations are excluded.. CLNPMID field from [PATH]/clinvar.vcf.gz">
##INFO=<ID=ClinVar_CLNSUBN,Number=.,Type=String,Description="Distinct submitting organisations for this variant, in SCV order. Spaces are rendered as underscores and the characters comma, semicolon, equals, pipe, ampersand, tilde, plus and percent are percent-encoded within values. VEP rewrites both comma and pipe to ampersand in a custom annotation, so after VEP the separator between entries reads as & instead of , while the ~ and + levels are unchanged.. CLNSUBN field from [PATH]/clinvar.vcf.gz">
##INFO=<ID=ClinVar_CLNRCV,Number=.,Type=String,Description="Per-condition (RCV) classifications, separated by commas. Subfields separated by ~: RCV ~ ClassificationType ~ ReviewStatus ~ Classification ~ Condition. The aggregate CLNSIG merges these. Spaces are rendered as underscores and the characters comma, semicolon, equals, pipe, ampersand, tilde, plus and percent are percent-encoded within values. VEP rewrites both comma and pipe to ampersand in a custom annotation, so after VEP the separator between entries reads as & instead of , while the ~ and + levels are unchanged.. CLNRCV field from [PATH]/clinvar.vcf.gz">
##INFO=<ID=ClinVar_SCI,Number=.,Type=String,Description="Aggregate somatic clinical impact for this single variant; multiple values are separated by a vertical bar. Values are separated by + and percent-encoded, so that they survive ingestion as a VEP custom annotation.. SCI field from [PATH]/clinvar.vcf.gz">
##INFO=<ID=ClinVar_SCIREVSTAT,Number=.,Type=String,Description="ClinVar review status of somatic clinical impact for the Variation ID. Values are separated by + and percent-encoded, so that they survive ingestion as a VEP custom annotation.. SCIREVSTAT field from [PATH]/clinvar.vcf.gz">
##INFO=<ID=ClinVar_SCIDN,Number=.,Type=String,Description="ClinVar's preferred disease name for the concept specified by disease identifiers in SCIDISDB. Values are separated by + and percent-encoded, so that they survive ingestion as a VEP custom annotation.. SCIDN field from [PATH]/clinvar.vcf.gz">
##INFO=<ID=ClinVar_SCIDISDB,Number=.,Type=String,Description="Tag-value pairs of disease database name and identifier submitted for somatic clinial impact classifications, e.g. MedGen:NNNNNN. Values are separated by + and percent-encoded, so that they survive ingestion as a VEP custom annotation.. SCIDISDB field from [PATH]/clinvar.vcf.gz">
